{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#962","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#962","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#962\",\"parent_revision\":\"03574d9122272a388674fe452df4a33ca51919f6d6fe194c1e8cc4ef89340751\",\"root_revision\":\"03574d9122272a388674fe452df4a33ca51919f6d6fe194c1e8cc4ef89340751\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nConvert the static workflow architecture diagram (.claude/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md from Issue #933) into a programmable pipeline engine. The pipeline should be: (1) a queryable dependency graph with typed edges between nodes, (2) a workflow analysis tool for reasoning about bottlenecks, missing edges, and redundant steps, (3) capable of selective step injection \u2014 depending on project type (Python CLI, FastAPI, TypeScript) and required validation harnesses, different steps get injected into the pipeline, (4) able to select validation harnesses that verify design intent was achieved for a specific project when executing plans. This builds on the SDLC layers concept (.claude/docs/sdlc-layers/) where Layer 1 is language and Layer 2 is stack profile. The pipeline engine would be Layer 0 \u2014 the execution infrastructure that composes Layer 1+2 steps into a project-specific pipeline.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | Workflow architecture diagram from #933 exists | DERIVABLE | `backlog_view(selector='#933')` or `.claude/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` |\\n| 2 | SDLC layers documentation with Layer 0/1/2 concepts | AVAILABLE | `.claude/docs/sdlc-layers/` |\\n| 3 | Existing pipeline dispatch mechanism in implement-feature | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/` |\\n| 4 | Graph library choice (networkx, graphlib stdlib, custom YAML DAG) | MISSING | Architecture decision not yet made |\\n| 5 | How to represent 'project type' discriminator (enum, profile file, CLI flag) | MISSING | Design decision not yet made |\\n\\nVerdict: BLOCKED \u2014 two architecture decisions (graph library, project type discriminator) must be made before implementation can begin. Recommend ecosystem-researcher to evaluate graph representation options.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP1 Feature. Major new infrastructure. High complexity. Touches implement-feature orchestration. Architecture decision required before scoping tasks.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- A queryable dependency graph with typed edges between pipeline nodes is defined (data structure or YAML manifest)\\n- A workflow analysis tool reasons about bottlenecks, missing edges, and redundant steps given the graph\\n- Selective step injection: given a project type (Python CLI, FastAPI, TypeScript), different steps are injected into the pipeline at the appropriate positions in the dependency graph\\n- Validation harness selection: the engine selects harnesses that verify design intent for the specific project type\\n- Integration with SDLC Layer 0 concept from `.claude/docs/sdlc-layers/` \u2014 Layer 0 is the execution infrastructure composing Layer 1 (language) and Layer 2 (stack profile) steps\\n- At minimum a proof-of-concept CLI or MCP tool that accepts a project type and returns an ordered task graph\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/` or new plugin \u2014 pipeline engine location TBD based on architecture decision\\n- `.claude/docs/sdlc-layers/` \u2014 update to reference Layer 0 engine\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/` \u2014 integrate with existing dispatch\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a workflow orchestrator, I need a programmable pipeline engine built on the workflow architecture diagram from #933 so I can compose project-type-specific SDLC pipelines with typed dependency edges and selective step injection instead of running static workflows.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **programmable pipeline engine \u2014 dependency graph with selective step injection** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User vision statement during #933 implementation \u2014 pipeline is infrastructure, not documentation\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"48c5f906708a372225e2aec5322abf107bb13cb4f7a1867d134eb425d04dfdb7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTEzfQ\"}"}